# Line endings for the files a Linux tool reads.
#
# This is a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true, so without these lines a
# checkout hands `tests/interop/run.sh` a CRLF shebang — which bash rejects
# outright — and hands the peers' configs and zone files to daemons running
# inside containers. A zone file is parsed byte for byte, so a stray \r is not
# cosmetic there either.
#
# Rust sources are deliberately left alone: rustfmt and the compiler do not
# care, and normalising them would be a whole-tree diff for nothing (§12's rule
# about never mixing a reformat into a change).
*.sh              text eol=lf
*.yml             text eol=lf
Dockerfile        text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*      text eol=lf
tests/interop/**  text eol=lf
